fix(memory): keep a hashless rejection's row bound to the bytes it read

Round 20 review, Grok 4.6: the rejection swept residue with the hash the
hashless door was bound to and then consumed the candidate with the
proposal's own -- empty for a proposal nobody could parse. The row it
kept when the sweep could not finish stayed on the hash it was created
with, so the next withdrawal swept for words nobody has, found the
original path empty, and retired the row over the copy it was kept for.
Both halves of the decision now name the same bytes.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
